00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:12.590
Now BHI is a turnkey
general contractor

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:14.750
that began as an
electrical contractor

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:18.170
and has grown into a company
that serves a civil, pipeline,

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:21.860
communication, electrical, and
renewable energy industries

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:23.980
across the United States.

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:25.730
CHRIS BAILEY: Now,
we've already mentioned

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:27.230
AppSheet a couple times.

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:30.330
And I realize that many people
are just learning about it.

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:33.680
So I wanted to start off by
giving a quick introduction

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:36.560
and overview to
what AppSheet is.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.990
AppSheet is a no code
application development

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:42.980
platform that enables
anyone to create apps fast.

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:45.320
At a high level, it's
a simple process.

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:47.450
First, you connect your data.

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:50.340
AppSheet can connect to a
wide variety of data sources,

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:53.690
including Excel files,
Google Sheets, cloud SQL,

00:01:53.690 --> 00:01:55.730
and on-premise databases.

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:58.610
Then you can customize your
app within the AppSheet editor,

00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:01.940
and create and adjust views,
workflows, notifications,

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:03.210
and more.

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:05.600
Finally, you can deploy
your applications out

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:08.300
to both mobile and
desktop devices.

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:10.070
And AppSheet does
an excellent job

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:13.350
of being responsive and working
on all of these devices.

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:15.680
So while AppSheet integrates
with a wide variety

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:18.830
of software, we found that
it is particularly powerful

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:20.830
when combined with G Suite.

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:23.570
The two products work
together in many ways.

00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:26.420
You can store app data
and content on drive.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:28.790
You can build an app
directly on top of Sheets,

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:32.210
and create, read, update,
and delete Sheets data

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:33.440
from the app.

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:36.980
You can open up Google
Meet, use Docs as templates,

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:39.260
create and update
calendar invites,

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:42.178
and extend your
forms functionality.

00:02:42.178 --> 00:02:44.470
There's a lot of goodness
that comes from using the two

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:45.860
platforms together.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:48.520
And I definitely
recommend exploring

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:53.610
how you can use them to solve
your business challenges.

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:56.420
So that's a high level
overview of what AppSheet is.

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:58.670
Now we want to shift
the topic and focus more

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:00.980
on the deskless
workforce and the ways

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:03.790
we can utilize AppSheet
to enable those teams.

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:07.190
80% of the global
workforce is deskless.

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:08.960
These are people
working in the field

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:12.110
and on the floor who have
to get up and move around,

00:03:12.110 --> 00:03:15.260
and don't spend the majority of
their time next to a computer.

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:18.290
Think of field technicians,
construction workers,

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:22.100
sales representatives, doctors,
nurses, event managers,

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:25.830
manufacturing specialists,
just to name a few.

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:29.100
More and more, we're seeing
deskless workers looking

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:31.920
to technology to find ways
to improve productivity

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:33.390
and efficiency.

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:34.890
And these challenges
they are facing

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:37.980
are different from those
faced by desk workers.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:40.650
For example, while it may be
very easy for someone sitting

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:44.700
at a desk to open up a new
Sheet, write up an invoice,

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:48.360
adjust margins and
formatting, that

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:51.420
can be much more difficult for
someone who's in the field,

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:54.600
as they may not have
a computer and they

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.685
may be on their
mobile phone or tablet

00:03:56.685 --> 00:03:58.560
where it's just trickier
to format a document

00:03:58.560 --> 00:03:59.970
and perform actions like that.

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:04.510
Now BHI's deskless
workers have been

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:07.280
using AppSheet in some
really interesting ways.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.280
So I actually want to
pass it over to Johnny

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:11.890
to talk about those
challenges they were facing,

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:15.490
and how they use
AppSheet to solve them.

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:17.269
JOHNNY HACKING: Awesome, thanks.

00:04:17.269 --> 00:04:19.209
So a challenge we
faced was we were

00:04:19.209 --> 00:04:21.100
required to submit
multiple inspection

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:24.790
forms on a daily basis
for one of our projects.

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:27.550
And current processes
just didn't work.

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:30.310
It was to fill out paper forms
in the field, and then later,

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:32.560
inputting that data to
send off from a computer

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:36.790
either at a hotel, job
trailer, or other location.

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:39.070
This needed to be done
for all inspections

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:43.210
that day, which were
multiple, sometimes 30 plus.

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:46.480
And we didn't have the manpower
to meet these requirements.

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:50.723
For this project, management
looked to IT for a solution.

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:53.140
Because hiring more people
would put the project's success

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:54.580
in jeopardy.

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:56.880
The current process
was not working.

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:58.720
Forms and spreadsheets
brought challenges

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:02.470
of managing data and workflows
across multiple jobs.

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:04.260
Developers can be costly.

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:06.820
And external solutions are
inflexible because it's never

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:08.410
just one external solution.

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:12.220
You know, we have multiple
divisions here at BHI,

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:13.920
and they all have
different needs.

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:16.360
Now BHI had just
migrated to G Suite

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:18.940
and was having great success
with the collaboration

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:19.900
it brought.

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:23.080
And that's when we found that
AppSheet on top of G Suite

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:25.090
gave us the ability
to take full advantage

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:27.070
of these digital platforms.

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:29.840
It gave us the offline
capability in an actual app,

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:32.170
and was easy for our
users in the field

00:05:32.170 --> 00:05:35.590
that are in very different
working conditions.

00:05:35.590 --> 00:05:38.230
AppSheet works seamless
with Google Sheets and Docs,

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:41.740
making it easy to push out
applications fast and simple.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:44.720
Actually, one of the apps in
the demo you will see later,

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:48.920
we made in a matter of hours
on a job site in a job trailer.

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:52.270
Customization of AppSheet
has helped us save money

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:55.380
because we are custom making
apps for specific jobs

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:59.180
that sometimes only get
used once for a project.

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:01.300
One thing to note is
that it isn't just IT

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:04.570
that is developing these apps,
but people from multiple teams

00:06:04.570 --> 00:06:06.990
that help make them better
because a lot of the times,

00:06:06.990 --> 00:06:08.740
they understand the
needs of their project

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:10.100
better than we do.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:11.680
IT is just brought
in as a final step

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:14.920
to review the app
before it goes live.

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:17.530
Since using AppSheet, I've
been told multiple times

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:19.985
on job sites how much
they love the apps,

00:06:19.985 --> 00:06:21.610
and to keep them
coming because they're

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:24.712
making their job a lot easier.

00:06:24.712 --> 00:06:27.070
Now AppSheet has solved
a lot of our problems

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:29.710
and transformed the way
we work as a company.

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:31.930
Its ease of use allows
for my small team

00:06:31.930 --> 00:06:34.240
to deploy apps that
meet the requirements

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:36.160
of multiple disciplines rapidly.

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:38.240
Forms that are
required on every job

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:40.570
are now digital and
filled out on the fly,

00:06:40.570 --> 00:06:43.360
with all the data being
stored in Google Drive.

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:45.520
Apps aren't just forms,
though, but something

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:47.770
that is tailored for each job.

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:50.590
We have ones that are used
across the entire company,

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:53.530
and others specific to projects
because of the information

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:56.120
gathered and reported
in real time.

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:59.170
This has cut costs by
reducing our overall IT

00:06:59.170 --> 00:07:02.830
budget by 10%, when we normally
paid that to other third party

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:04.350
softwares.

00:07:04.350 --> 00:07:08.170
And an example is some quality
inspections on electrical work

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:11.668
was taking up to two hours
to do one inspection.

00:07:11.668 --> 00:07:13.210
By the time everything
was filled out

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:15.670
and inputted into
a PDF, combined

00:07:15.670 --> 00:07:18.490
with pictures taken
onsite, and emailed

00:07:18.490 --> 00:07:21.400
to the client on a daily
basis from a computer

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:23.620
back in the office.

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:27.130
Not only did our apps allow
this to happen in the field,

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:30.790
but they also cut down these
inspection forms from two hours

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:32.260
to six minutes.

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:33.760
This was a solution
to our challenge

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:35.560
in the previous slide.

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:38.290
The result was money
saved and we're

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:42.420
able to meet the
job requirements.

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:44.710
AppSheet has also
given us more time.

00:07:44.710 --> 00:07:47.680
With two of our AppSheet
apps, from one department

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:50.780
completely freed up
20 to 30 hours a week.

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:53.110
This time was generally spent
on printing and scanning

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:57.100
forms to manually inputting
data into a spreadsheet

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:58.850
so that it could be analyzed.

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:03.520
Now our workflows do this
in a matter of minutes.

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:06.250
We are now making decisions
on data that's happening now,

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:08.440
versus what happened
two weeks ago.

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:10.570
The best part about
this is our employees

00:08:10.570 --> 00:08:12.460
are coming up with
new, innovative ways

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:15.970
we can use AppSheet, which isn't
happening in conference rooms,

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:19.900
but across construction
sites all over the country.

