And if you try to move
on to the next step

00:11:57.590 --> 00:12:00.110
without filling those
out, you'll get an error.

00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:02.390
And you can also set
additional parameters

00:12:02.390 --> 00:12:04.760
on those requirements
like, specifying

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:08.390
that it has to be an email or a
number or something like that.

00:12:11.182 --> 00:12:13.390
JOHNNY HACKING: And then
we're going to get down here

00:12:13.390 --> 00:12:15.160
with the employee signature.

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:19.617
Just so you know that if you are
on a tablet or a smart device,

00:12:19.617 --> 00:12:21.700
and you click on that,
you'll be able to just draw

00:12:21.700 --> 00:12:24.620
with your finger or
a stylus or whatever,

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:28.810
and actually capture people's
real life signatures.

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:31.690
And then at the very bottom,
you can fill in an email address

00:12:31.690 --> 00:12:33.730
if, for some reason,
you need it to email

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:38.992
a copy of this Near Miss to that
person for reporting purposes.

00:12:38.992 --> 00:12:39.700
You fill that in.

00:12:39.700 --> 00:12:41.830
Once it saves,
AppSheet has a workflow

00:12:41.830 --> 00:12:45.020
that combines this information,
puts it into a PDF,

00:12:45.020 --> 00:12:48.260
and emails it off
to that person.

00:12:48.260 --> 00:12:50.723
Now that we've hit
Save, you can see all

00:12:50.723 --> 00:12:52.890
that it's been added with
the other Near Misses that

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:54.320
have been filled out.

00:12:54.320 --> 00:12:55.370
And it's right here.

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:57.940
And we have done our job.

00:12:57.940 --> 00:12:59.600
CHRIS BAILEY: Now,
there's one more app

00:12:59.600 --> 00:13:02.540
that I think is really clever
that we want to show you.

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:04.605
The Time Entry app.

00:13:04.605 --> 00:13:05.980
JOHNNY HACKING:
So yeah, this app

00:13:05.980 --> 00:13:09.070
is really interesting because
COVID had just happened.

00:13:09.070 --> 00:13:11.470
And we needed to
create something

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:13.270
that would meet all
the requirements

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:17.410
of social distancing and not
to touch as many surfaces

00:13:17.410 --> 00:13:20.570
as possible as we could
for this job site.

00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:22.660
And to keep track
of time, people

00:13:22.660 --> 00:13:24.898
would just click on a
tablet and punch it in.

00:13:24.898 --> 00:13:25.940
Well, not with this case.

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:28.410
We created a solution
so we didn't have to.

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:32.220
On Setup here, each employee
will be in the list.

00:13:32.220 --> 00:13:33.190
And we'd add employees.

00:13:33.190 --> 00:13:36.640
And we'd give everyone a
bar code that was a sticker.

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:39.690
And we'd put that
underneath their hardhat.

00:13:39.690 --> 00:13:43.290
From there, every day, the
person in charge of time

00:13:43.290 --> 00:13:45.180
would click on Check In.

00:13:45.180 --> 00:13:47.520
And what that would
do is it would open up

00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:49.627
the scanned section.

00:13:49.627 --> 00:13:51.960
And if you were on a tablet,
it would open up the camera

00:13:51.960 --> 00:13:52.590
itself.

00:13:52.590 --> 00:13:54.690
And it would just stay
open all the time.

00:13:54.690 --> 00:13:56.940
What would happen is when
a bar code is filled in,

00:13:56.940 --> 00:14:01.200
or you hold their hardhat,
the bar code sticker,

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:04.530
the camera will recognize
that, fill in the bar code.

00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:06.420
It will save it,
and automatically

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:07.810
go to the next one.

00:14:07.810 --> 00:14:10.590
And it will just keep doing this
all day until that person would

00:14:10.590 --> 00:14:13.860
come back and get the tablet, at
which everyone has been clocked

00:14:13.860 --> 00:14:17.850
in for the day, not having to
touch the iPad or the tablet

00:14:17.850 --> 00:14:20.052
or anything.

00:14:20.052 --> 00:14:21.510
CHRIS BAILEY: At
this point, you're

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:23.820
likely curious to see what
these applications look

00:14:23.820 --> 00:14:25.210
like on the back end.

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:27.390
So I'm going to open
up the AppSheet editor

00:14:27.390 --> 00:14:30.207
and show you what it looks like.

00:14:30.207 --> 00:14:32.790
So let's look at the Time Entry
app that Johnny just showed us

00:14:32.790 --> 00:14:35.620
and see what it looks
like behind the scenes.

00:14:35.620 --> 00:14:39.180
Now all of that apps data is
hosted in this Google Sheet.

00:14:39.180 --> 00:14:42.060
It has two tabs, the
first with a simple table

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:44.560
that will update as
people clock in and out,

00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:47.080
and the second with the
employees emails and associated

00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:48.510
bar codes.

00:14:48.510 --> 00:14:51.330
To create an app, all you'd
have to do to get started

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:53.070
is to pull up AppSheet
and connect it

00:14:53.070 --> 00:14:54.940
to a spreadsheet like this.

00:14:54.940 --> 00:14:58.500
So let's see what it looks
like in the App editor.

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:00.360
This is the AppSheet editor.

00:15:00.360 --> 00:15:03.527
Over here on the right, you can
see a live preview of the app.

00:15:03.527 --> 00:15:05.110
And you can switch
to different views,

00:15:05.110 --> 00:15:09.090
whether you want to see phone,
tablet, or desktop views.

00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:12.820
On the far left, we have the
main menu of Edit Options.

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:15.460
The key ones you need to know
when you're getting started

00:15:15.460 --> 00:15:18.570
are Info, which gives
high level information

00:15:18.570 --> 00:15:21.780
about your app, Data, which
lets you build and update

00:15:21.780 --> 00:15:25.500
your tables, columns, and
sizes, UX, where you can adjust

00:15:25.500 --> 00:15:27.980
the look and feel of
the app, and Behavior,

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:32.070
where you can set up actions,
workflows, and reports.

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:36.210
Let me highlight a few
key features of this app.

00:15:36.210 --> 00:15:39.560
So when we go to Data Tables
in this time tracker app,

00:15:39.560 --> 00:15:41.930
we can see that the same
tables in the spreadsheet

00:15:41.930 --> 00:15:43.790
are also listed out here.

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:46.260
Timesheet and Setup.

00:15:46.260 --> 00:15:49.230
When we select View Columns,
we see that all the columns

00:15:49.230 --> 00:15:50.700
were added as well.

00:15:50.700 --> 00:15:52.200
There's also some
additional columns

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:56.090
that have been created to
add functionality to the app.

00:15:56.090 --> 00:15:58.850
And several of them,
if we look here,

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:00.920
include formulas that
we've added to help

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:02.120
run the logic of the app.

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:09.340
Next, if you wanted to adjust
the look and feel of the app,

00:16:09.340 --> 00:16:12.760
you can go to UX Brand
and easily change your app

00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:15.490
to light mode or
dark mode, and adjust

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:18.490
your colors, which you
can see being updated

00:16:18.490 --> 00:16:19.630
in the live preview here.

00:16:22.510 --> 00:16:24.930
Now let's say you wanted to
have an automated report sent

00:16:24.930 --> 00:16:28.500
to the payroll manager that
showed how long each employee

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:30.390
worked that day.

00:16:30.390 --> 00:16:32.970
That report is simple to set up.

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:37.840
You can go to Behavior,
Reports, and select New Report.

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:39.230
Here, we've already created one.

00:16:39.230 --> 00:16:41.070
So let's just open
that up to give you

00:16:41.070 --> 00:16:42.820
an idea of what that
report can look like.

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:49.130
So Daily, at 8:00
PM Mountain Time,

00:16:49.130 --> 00:16:53.300
use the Today's Timetable,
which, just so you know,

00:16:53.300 --> 00:16:58.430
is a virtual table or slice
that we created within this app.

00:16:58.430 --> 00:17:01.110
We don't have to set
additional conditions.

00:17:01.110 --> 00:17:04.119
So let's leave
that section blank.

00:17:04.119 --> 00:17:05.940
And do this.

00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:08.819
Let's send an email
to these two addresses

00:17:08.819 --> 00:17:12.890
with this information,
and a note

00:17:12.890 --> 00:17:14.780
here that you can
have piped text to.

00:17:17.400 --> 00:17:19.349
And let's also
send a text message

00:17:19.349 --> 00:17:22.480
so that they know the
report is in their inbox.

00:17:22.480 --> 00:17:24.180
So you update all this.

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:26.849
And after that, you click
Save, test the report out

00:17:26.849 --> 00:17:28.620
once or twice, and
start using it.

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:34.610
Now I'm going to stop the demo
here because, unfortunately, we

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:37.840
